;; spec:   stdlib §2.3 (Div), §7 L30, plan R3 (Num loses `/`)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  cannot unify (Ratio i64) with i64
;; `/` is not a method of `Num`: it is `Div`'s, in every module, so a generic function whose
;; bound is `Num t` and whose body divides two `t`s has `/` of `Div`, not the machine's
;; division (the checker adds the `Div` bound to the function's own). Called at `i64` the
;; quotient is a ratio, which is not the `t` the function promises: the call is the error.
;; Integer division is `quot`. Case 877 is the same function at floats, which is accepted.
(defun d (a: t b: t) :where ((Num t)) -> t (/ a b))

(defun main () -> i64 (d 6 3))
